# Tofu — Install Guide

This page covers everything beyond the one-line install in the README:
all installer flags, manual conda steps, the GLIBC trap, and recovery
recipes when something goes wrong.

For the happy path, just run the one-command install from the README.
You only need this page if that didn't work or you want full control.

---

## Installer Flags

The `install.sh` (Linux/macOS) and `install.py` (any OS) installers share
the same flags. Pass them to either; they have identical behavior.

### Common flags

| Flag | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `--api-key sk-xxx` | Pre-configure your LLM API key (writes to `.env`) |
| `--port 8080` | Server port (default `15000`) |
| `--no-launch` | Install only, don't start the server |
| `--dir <path>` | Install directory (default `~/tofu`) |
| `--with-docling` | Also install Docling for layout-aware PDF parsing (~2 GB; pulls torch + model weights) |
| `--reset-env` | **Destructive.** Delete the existing conda env and rebuild from scratch |
| `--force-sqlite` | Skip PostgreSQL entirely; pin `TOFU_DB_BACKEND=sqlite` in `.env` |
| `--skip-playwright` | Skip Chromium binary install (saves ~150 MB if you don't need page rendering) |

### Recovery / advanced flags

You shouldn't normally need these — they exist for hosts where the default
flow misbehaves.

| Flag | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `--env <name>` | Conda env name (default `tofu`) |
| `--python 3.12` | Python version for the env |
| `--no-update-conda` | Skip the conda self-update step |
| `--pg-major <N>` | Force a specific PostgreSQL major (e.g. `17`). Default tries 18 → 17 → 16 |
| `--reinit-pgdata` | If `data/pgdata/` was created by a different PG major, back it up and re-initdb (otherwise the installer auto-falls-back to SQLite, preserving data) |
| `--min-conda <N>` | Minimum acceptable conda major version (default `24`) |
| `--force-sibling-conda` | Always install our own private Miniforge as a project sibling, even if a usable conda exists |

### Docker path

```bash
git clone https://github.com/rangehow/ToFu.git && cd ToFu
docker compose up -d
```

All data persists in named Docker volumes. No flags needed.

